meta {
  name: Update Alternative Style
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/styles/:id
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
  id: {{alternativeStyleId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "alternative_point_style",
    "sldContent": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><StyledLayerDescriptor xmlns=\"http://www.opengis.net/sld\" xmlns:ogc=\"http://www.opengis.net/ogc\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" version=\"1.0.0\"><NamedLayer><Name>alternative_point_style</Name><UserStyle><FeatureTypeStyle><Rule><PointSymbolizer><Graphic><Mark><WellKnownName>square</WellKnownName><Fill><CssParameter name=\"fill\">#a8501e</CssParameter></Fill></Mark><Size>10</Size></Graphic></PointSymbolizer></Rule></FeatureTypeStyle></UserStyle></NamedLayer></StyledLayerDescriptor>"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('alternativeStyleId', res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` and `alternativeStyleId` are set.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, body reflects updated `sldContent` for the alternative style.

  **Note:** Parallel to `update-style.bru`, but targets the alternative style via `{{alternativeStyleId}}` instead of `{{styleId}}`. Same caveat: PATCH is not supported on Styles — the controller returns 405.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | Alternative Style record updated in `portal_backend` DB |
  | Config Adapter | — (GeoServer style is re-uploaded when the parent DataSet is re-released) |
  | External System | — |
}
